hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16741","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us that an old man from Banu Salit informed him, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to speak to him about captives taken from us in the jahiliyya, and he was sitting with a circle surrounding him, speaking to the people, upon him a coarse Qitri izar; he said: I heard him say, pointing with his finger: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim, he does not wrong him nor forsake him; taqwa is here, taqwa is here, meaning in the heart."
